nodes.rationale:
On Bolna, mechanisms read from bundle flags were fully right 1 time in 4:
- ambient_noise_track: no mixing code in OSS;
- use_fillers: a prompt note, and the audio path is dead code;
- synthesizer.caching: lasts one call only.
Structure inferences were 5/5 correct and docs-led ones 13/14. A flag shows that a feature is exposed, not how it works.

nodes.title:
Before inferring a closed vendor's architecture, sweep its full docs dump (llms-full / sitemap) against a fixed checklist:
- speech-to-speech mode;
- eager or speculative turn-taking;
- barge-in trigger;
- hangup modes;
- tools (incl. web search);
- multi-agent handoff;
- RAG placement;
- language ID and switching;
- telemetry;
- defaults.

Bolna language switching in code is a dedicated judge LLM:
- default claude-haiku-4-5 via LiteLLM, with a Bedrock ap-south-1 option;
- fed by a parallel streaming LID recognizer (Sarvam or Soniox);
- hedged duplicate request at 1.8 s, 6 s cap;
- speculative follow-up in the target language;
- per-language handoff clips cached across calls.
This corrects the l4a description 'code-switching is a prompt'.

Hosted-only Bolna mechanisms that the open code cannot decide:
- whether and where ambient noise is mixed;
- whether hosted fillers play audio;
- the hosted ws route and run id;
- the hosted Deepgram MIP opt-out value;
- the model behind the hosted language judge;
- the RabbitMQ scheduler's dedupe, opt-out and calling-window behaviour.

nodes.closes_when:
Account-phase capture closes it:
- a stereo recording of a default-agent call with ambient_noise and use_fillers on;
- the execution log's other_latencies model fields for language_switch / hangup_check / voicemail_check;
- the messy-CSV batch result (predictions P04a-P05).
